Z||000002||HAGS||01-26-2001||06:07 AM||||Well unless I can get a Fiero that runs like a new car for under 4k cash then I dont think I am...even if I do find a good deal my family would kill me.  I've put so much time into my 86 Sport Coupe and it doesnt like me...I love it but its drawn the last straw!! I will probably try to get sell it for $750, I payed $800, replaced all 3 mounts, alternator, 4 month old 60 month battery, new throttle body, new spark plugs, new O2 sensor, new head gasket/bolts(unopened).<P>*might* need new starter<BR>*most likely* needs lifters<BR>*most likely* needs poly bushings<BR>right rear cradle connection broke, bolt still in its hole but cradle dropped...being held up with bungy cords...<BR>rear tires need thrust realignment, handling was awesome until recently, dont know what happend...<P>I know its asking a miracle for such a POS but thats what I expect to get for trade-in at dealer, my mom works there and they are the ones that sold it to me...burnt on my first used car!!  I was too much of a fanatic and too excited about owning one I never returned it with the melon law...||||reg||1
Z||000003||HAGS||01-26-2001||06:12 AM||||I was looking at a guys 92 Firebird and he offered $1200 for my Fiero but that was before the knocking....and I think he was thinking I got good gas mileage but at the time I was only getting about 10, with the new plugs I got a little over 20 on 100 mile highway drive doing 80+||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||01-26-2001||09:16 AM||||The Focus ZX3 is a cool little car -- but I'm guessing you'll be looking at payments of over $200/mo to lease one and $240 or more to buy it outright.  That's a lot of jack!!!<P>Why not buy a nice, well-maintained 87 or 88 Coupe to drive while you're ironing the bugs out of the 85 GT?  You'll get your money back when you sell the Coupe if you don't rag on it.<P>Besides, the other people on this Forum aren't going to let you buy a Focus anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
