Z||000006||Oreif||01-26-2001||10:03 AM||||If you need to get a car that is "reliable", My suggestion would be to get a used car between 1-3 years old. Most cars in that range are probably lease vehicles. You could even look at a Saturn. Most used saturns come with at least a 1 year warranty (if bought at a saturn dealer) and the customer service they provide is excellent. The SC2 has a dual overhead cam engine, looks sporty, (unlike a focus), and could save you $1000's. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheHans||01-26-2001||11:20 AM||||I would reccommend a Saturn it is one of my 3 cars and by far the most reliable. Not knocking the Fiero, but the Saturn has a wonderful 1.9l that is good on gas and has given me no trouble since 94. It's like you don't drive the Porsche to work everyday. ha.<BR>Plus it's easier to hide the smell of the spilled bong water in the Saturn. j/j. ||||reg||10
